    "diff_hunk": "@@ -23227,6 +23259,114 @@ interface <dfn>HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils</dfn> {\n   </div>\n \n \n+  <h5>Link type \"<dfn><code data-x=\"rel-modulepreload\">modulepreload</code></dfn>\"</h5>\n+\n+  <p>The <code data-x=\"rel-modulepreload\">modulepreload</code> keyword may be used with\n+  <code>link</code> elements. This keyword creates an <span>external resource link</span>. This\n+  keyword is <span>body-ok</span>.</p>\n+\n+  <p>The <code data-x=\"rel-modulepreload\">modulepreload</code> keyword is a specialized alternative\n+  to the <code data-x=\"rel-preload\">preload</code> keyword, with a processing model geared toward\n+  preloading <span data-x=\"module script\">module scripts</span>. In particular, it <span\n+  data-x=\"fetch a module script graph\">fetches</span> the entire module script graph rooted at the\n+  given URL, and places it into the appropriate <span data-x=\"concept-document-module-map\">module\n+  map</span> for later evaluation. (In contrast, a similar <span>external resource link</span> using\n+  the <code data-x=\"rel-preload\">preload</code> keyword would only fetch a single module script\n+  resource, and would place it in the preload cache, without affecting the document's <span\n+  data-x=\"concept-document-module-map\">module map</span>.)</p>\n+\n+  <div w-nodev>\n+\n+  <p>The following contains are the appropriate times to fetch the resource for such a link:</p>\n+\n+  <ul>\n+   <li><p>When the <span>external resource link</span> is created on a <code>link</code> element\n+   that is already <span>browsing-context connected</span>.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li><p>When the <span>external resource link</span>'s <code>link</code> element <span>becomes\n+   browsing-context connected</span>.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li><p>When the <code data-x=\"attr-link-href\">href</code> attribute of the <code>link</code>\n+   element of an <span>external resource link</span> that is already <span>browsing-context\n+   connected</span> is changed.</p></li>\n+  </ul>\n+\n+  </div>\n+\n+  <p class=\"note\">Unlike some other link relations, changing the relevant attributes (such as <code\n+  data-x=\"attr-link-as\">as</code>, <code data-x=\"attr-link-crossorigin\">crossorigin</code>, and\n+  <code data-x=\"attr-link-referrerpolicy\">referrerpolicy</code>) of such a <code>link</code>\n+  attribute does not trigger a new fetch. This is because the document's <span\n+  data-x=\"concept-document-module-map\">module map</span> has already been populated by a previous\n+  fetch, and so re-fetching would be pointless.</p>\n+\n+  <div w-nodev>\n+\n+  <p>To fetch the resource for such a link:</p>\n+\n+  <ol>\n+   <li><p>If the <code data-x=\"attr-link-href\">href</code> attribute's value is the empty string,\n+   then abort these steps.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li><p>If the <code data-x=\"attr-link-as\">as</code> attribute is specified and its value is not\n+   one of \"<code data-x=\"\">script</code>\", \"<code data-x=\"\">worker</code>\", \"<code\n+   data-x=\"\">sharedworker</code>\", or \"<code data-x=\"\">serviceworker</code>\", then <span>queue a\n+   task</span> on the <span>networking task source</span> to <span data-x=\"concept-event-fire\">fire\n+   an event</span> named <code data-x=\"event-error\">error</code> at the <code>link</code> element,\n+   and abort these steps.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li><p>Let <var>destination</var> be the value of the <code data-x=\"attr-link-as\">as</code>\n+   attribute, if it is specified, or \"<code data-x=\"\">script</code>\" otherwise.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li><p><span data-x=\"parse a url\">Parse</span> the <span>URL</span> given by the <code\n+   data-x=\"attr-link-href\">href</code> attribute, relative to the element's <span>node\n+   document</span>. If that fails, then abort these steps. Otherwise, let <var>url</var> be the\n+   <span>resulting URL record</span>.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li><p>Let <var>credentials mode</var> be the <span>module script credentials mode</span> for the\n+   <code data-x=\"attr-link-crossorigin\">crossorigin</code> attribute.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li>\n+    <p><span>Fetch a module script graph</span> given <var>url</var>, the <code>link</code>\n+    element's <code>node document</code>'s <span>relevant settings object</span>,\n+    <var>destination</var>, the value of the <code>link</code> element's <code\n+    data-x=\"attr-link-nonce\">nonce</code> content attribute,\n+    \"<code data-x=\"\">not parser-inserted</code>\", and <var>credentials\n+    mode</var>.</p>\n+\n+    <p>To <span data-x=\"fetching-scripts-perform-fetch\">perform the fetch</span> given\n+    <var>request</var>, perform the following steps:</p>\n+\n+    <ol>\n+     <li><p>Set <var>request</var>'s <span data-x=\"concept-request-referrer-policy\">referrer\n+     policy</span> to the current state of the <code>link</code> element's <code\n+     data-x=\"attr-link-referrerpolicy\">referrerpolicy</code> attribute.</p></li>\n+\n+     <!-- integrity?? https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2382 -->\n+\n+     <li><p><span data-x=\"concept-fetch\">Fetch</span> <var>request</var>, and asynchronously wait\n+     to run the remaining steps as part of fetch's <span>process response</span> for the <span",
